From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:15:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s5l8960x: Add Lightning charging to the A7
 iPads

iBoot leaves the D2089's input-current limit at 100 mA (0x4c0 = 0x02),
so an A7 iPad drains on a cable. Describe, in the iPad Air's and the
iPad mini 2's shared files (the iPad mini 3 includes the latter), the
D2089's PMU event controller, the Lightning charger on the PMIC with the
PMU line (112) and ADC done (89), and the Tristar (CBTL1610) at 0x1a.
Link the charger to the USB device controller, which reports the host's
allowance to it and whose data role the charger sets.

Only the wiring differs, as Apple's device trees give it (iOS 12.5.7
and 12.5.8): every A7 iPad has a pmu,d2089 at i2c0 0x3c and a
tristar,cbtl1610 at 0x1a; the PMU interrupt is AP GPIO 103 on the J71,
J72 and J73 and GPIO 21 on the J85-J87 and J85m-J87m, and the Tristar
sits on I2C2 on the iPad Air and on I2C0 on the iPad mini 2 and 3.

The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input on all of them.
The maximum is 1050 mA instead, the highest limit measured on an A7:
code 0x4e charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA under the desktop,
at 35.8-36.1 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run on a powered hub port,
and the limit went back to 0x02 on unplug. A higher maximum waits for a
measurement.

No source events, as on the iPad Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of the
connection state sees plug and unplug.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi  | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 130 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
index 5e465a16a..cbbe6ab57 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-air1.dtsi
@@ -136,3 +136,68 @@ cs42l81: audio-codec@0 {
 		#sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Lightning charging, at the D2089's registers as iOS 12
+ * AppleD2089PMUPowerSource uses them: connection and charger state at
+ * 0x60, the input-current limit at 0x4c0, the ADC at 0x500.
+ */
+&{/soc/i2c@20a110000/pmic@3c} {
+	/* The PMU event line, from the ADT pmu node: AP GPIO 103. */
+	pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
+		compatible = "apple,d2089-pmic-gpio";
+		interrupt-controller;
+		#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&pinctrl 103 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The ADT's charger node allows 0x960 = 2400 mA of input on every iPad Air.
+	 * The maximum here is the highest input limit measured on an A7
+	 * so far: 1050 mA (0x4e) charged a J72's battery at +279 to +423 mA
+	 * under the desktop, at 36 C, in thisiscamk's ten-minute run.
+	 */
+	tristar_charger: charger@60 {
+		compatible = "apple,d2089-tristar-charger";
+		reg = <0x60 0x0d>, <0x4c0 0x01>, <0x500 0x04>;
+		reg-names = "status", "control", "adc";
+		interrupt-parent = <&pmu_events>;
+		/*
+		 * The PMU line and ADC done. No source events, as on the iPad
+		 * Air 2: the charger's 100 ms poll of 0x60 sees plug and unplug.
+		 */
+		interrupts = <112 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			     <89 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		apple,tristar = <&tristar>;
+		input-current-limit-microamp = <1050000>;
+
+		/* The charger decides when USB data may come on. */
+		port {
+			tristar_charger_usb: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&usbdev_role>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c2 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/* The Lightning port controller, from the ADT i2c2/tristar node. */
+	tristar: port-controller@1a {
+		compatible = "nxp,cbtl1610";
+		reg = <0x1a>;
+	};
+};
+
+/* Tell the Lightning charger what the USB host allows. */
+&usbdev {
+	usb-psy-name = "lightning";
+	usb-role-switch;
+
+	port {
+		usbdev_role: endpoint {
+			remote-endpoint = <&tristar_charger_usb>;
+		};
+	};
+};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
index c7a95fc01..09ebe61e9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s5l8960x-mini2.dtsi
@@ -92,3 +92,68 @@ rtc_offset: rtc-offset@4 {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Lightning charging, at the D2089's registers as iOS 12
+ * AppleD2089PMUPowerSource uses them: connection and charger state at
+ * 0x60, the input-current limit at 0x4c0, the ADC at 0x500.
+ */
+&{/soc/i2c@20a110000/pmic@3c} {
+	/* The PMU event line, from the ADT pmu node: AP GPIO 21. */
+	pmu_events: interrupt-controller {
+		compatible = "apple,d2089-pmic-gpio";
